From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:57:48 +0200
Subject: media: cedrus: add VC-1 decoding support

Add a stateless VC-1 decoder to the Cedrus driver, for the Simple, Main
and Advanced profiles (WMV3 and WVC1): progressive, frame interlaced
and field interlaced pictures of all types, the variable quantizer and
transform modes, intensity compensation, range reduction, reduced
resolution coding (MULTIRES), overlap smoothing and the seven
bitplanes. The register programming follows the Allwinner vendor
library.

The hardware parses the macroblock layer: the driver programs the
picture header state, starts the bit reader on the first macroblock and
passes the decoded bitplanes. It also handles the slices of Advanced
profile pictures by itself. It detects the slice start codes and reads
SLICE_ADDR and PIC_HEADER_FLAG, but needs to be told how long the
repeated picture header is, so the driver exposes the slice parameters
control to get it.

Facts the driver has to apply, found by comparing the hardware with the
SMPTE reference decoder:
 - Overlap smoothing applies to all macroblocks when PQUANT >= 9, also
   in Advanced profile I and BI pictures, which then have no CONDOVER.
 - In interlaced frame pictures, active overlap smoothing makes the
   hardware write garbage, whatever the configuration. Such pictures
   are decoded without overlap smoothing, which only leaves vertical
   block edges unsmoothed; interlaced encoders don't seem to use it.
 - Pictures narrower than 8 macroblocks get wrong co-located motion
   vectors in the last macroblock column, and pictures 2 macroblocks
   wide don't decode at all, so widths below 128 are rejected, and
   below 256 in MULTIRES sequences, whose pictures may be half as wide.
 - A reduced resolution (RESPIC) picture decodes as a picture of its
   coded size, which the frame size, picture size and bitplane size
   must give, into the top-left corner of the buffers. The vendor
   library always programs the size of the sequence and gets it wrong.

Streams the hardware cannot decode are rejected when the controls are
set: the Complex profile and pre-release WMV3 (RES_RTM_FLAG = 0), whose
macroblock layer is coded differently.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
